odule with options: metric ('cosine','pearson'), apply normalization if needed, and a shrinkage term for low-support pairs.\\n\\n7) Neighborhood selection\\n- Top-k selection exists, but pruning semantics could be clearer (prune zeros/negatives). Implement explicit handling: drop neighbors with similarity <= 0 if requested, and make top_k a strict bound on number of neighbors. Preserve deterministic neighbor sampling if needed.\\n\\n8) Prediction formula\\n- The implemented formula resembles user-based deviance with user means but uses item-item similarities and user-rated neighbors; this should be clearly documented as an explicit item-based CF variant. If user-based CF is desired, refactor to compute user-user similarities and use them to predict: pred = user_mean + sum(sim * (rating_of_neighbor - neighbor_mean)) / sum(|sim|). Also ensure global baseline option works as described.\\n- Clip predictions to rating scale (1-5) is present, good.\\n\\n9) Cold-start handling\\n- There is some handling: if a user has no rated items in training, falls back to user mean; if test user/item is unseen, the code drops the row, which is deterministic but not ideal. Implement explicit cold-start fallback to global mean or respective baseline and ensure deterministic behavior.\\n\\n10) Evaluation\\n- RMSE is computed, but MAE is missing; optionally compute coverage. Implement MAE and coverage metrics as part of evaluation.\\n\\n11) Hyperparameters and reproducibility\\n- Hyperparameters like k (neighbors), similarity_metric, shrinkage, and baseline option are not exposed; defaults are hard-coded. Expose a clean API (e.g., function arguments or a config object) and provide sensible defaults. Keep random seed for all stochastic steps.\\n\\n12) Outputs and modularity\\n- The code is monolithic; there is no clean API with data_loader, preprocessor, cf_model, evaluator modules as requested. Print basic dataset stats is missing. Add modular structure and optional CSV export for predictions; ensure there is a clear API.\\n\\nRecommendations to reach a robust 90+% implementation:\\n- Implement a modular loader supporting ml-100k and ml-1m with 0-based indices and CSR matrices; provide functions to get n_users, n_items, sparsity, and mappings.\\n- Build a CSR training matrix and compute global_mean, user_means, item_means; allow baseline usage flag.\\n- Implement a parameterizable CF model with mode ('user'|'item'), similarity metric ('cosine','pearson'), and shrinkage. Compute similarity with proper normalization and shrinkage for low-support pairs.\\n- Implement explicit top-k neighbor selection with deterministic handling and clear pruning rules (e.g., drop non-positive similarities if requested).\\n- Implement both user-based and item-based predictions and clearly choose one based on mode; ensure the formula matches the spec and baseline option.\\n- Add evaluation for RMSE and MAE and optional coverage; expose a small evaluation summary.\\n- Refactor into modules: data_loader.py, preprocessor.py, cf_model.py, evaluator.py with a clear API.\\n- Expose hyperparameters (k, similarity_metric, shrinkage, baseline) and seeds, and log dataset stats at startup.\\n\\nIf you want, I can provide concrete code sketches or a minimal refactor to meet each requirement.", is_satisfactory=False)\
